/etc stands for Et Cetera.
Historically held miscellaneous system files.
Now contains static configuration data.
Stores system-wide settings and scripts.

passwd: Stores user account information.

shadow: Contains encrypted password hashes.

group: Defines system groups and members.

fstab: Lists static filesystem mount points.

hosts: Maps hostnames to IP addresses locally.

resolv.conf: Configures DNS name servers.

hostname: Sets the system's network name.

cron.d: Holds scheduled task definitions.

ssh: Contains Secure Shell server settings